{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004643-what-really-happened-during-the-2016-election","id":1004643,"title":"What really happened during the 2016 election...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-17T14:44:50-08:00","id":1004643,"title":"What really happened during the 2016 election...","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The 2016 Election and the Great Meme War</b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;It's still sinking in; we literally memed the absolute MADMAN into the White House.&quot;</i><br /> Anonymous user in one of the darkest corners of the Internet.<br /> <br /> <br /> The nomination of Donald Trump took everyone by surprise, from his opponents to his supporters and even himself. Few imagined at the beginning of his run that he would become President, least of all the Virtual Adepts who hold the most responsibility for putting him there.<br /> <br /> In early 2015 a hacker in the Virtual Adepts stumbled across a prognostication timeline from the New World Order. Their plans, which began with the election of Jeb Bush to the presidency in 2016, then involved several wars and by 2100 the unification of the world.<br /> <br /> To say that the timeline was... optimistic would be an understatement at the least, but many Virtual Adepts were quite worried. After numerous arguments and debate, a large group of Adepts decided that the best course of action would be to do whatever they could to prevent Jeb Bush's election as the 45th president of the United States. Such an event would scramble the NWO's timeline and perhaps push back several key events by years or even decades.<br /> <br /> The Adepts then spent more time arguing and fighting over the best way to do it. Some suggested backing a more moderate candidate. Others considered trying to dig up or create dirt on Jeb Bush. Yet others wanted to back a Democratic candidate such as Bernie Sanders and get him into office. All arguments however ended when millionaire Donald Trump threw his hat into the Republican primary ring.<br /> <br /> The Virtual Adepts smiled as one. They had their chaos candidate. Some objected to the racist statements he had already released, but they were laughed at. After all, it's not as if what he said mattered - Trump would <i>never</i> get into the White House; his campaign would eventually go down in flames one way or another. But, the Virtual Adepts hoped, perhaps he could drag down Jeb Bush's campaign with him. And so they began uniting their powers behind Donald Trump.<br /> <br /> Trump's early successes caught the Technocracy off guard. Their estimates proved to be wrong time and time again. He seemed impervious to his own remarks, saying things that would have caused any other candidate's campaign at any point in history to explode. Time and again he proved pundits and the greatest of the Technocracy's future modalists wrong. As one, and then another of his opponents retired from the race, the NWO scrambled to find out what the secret behind Donald Trump's success was.<br /> <br /> That's when they discovered the memes and for the first time saw the hands of the Virtual Adepts behind the candidate.<br /> <br /> The NWO had first encountered internet memes several decades earlier, but had written them off as too chaotic to be of any particular use. They had seen early memes such as All Your Base, the Dancing Baby and later the Rickroll and lolcats. For the NWO at the time, memes were nothing more than simple tools to keep the populace entertained. They never imagined the kind of power that memes, properly weaponized and directed could hold.<br /> <br /> In its support for Donald Trump, the Virtual Adepts unleashed a volley of such weaponized memes across the internet. Many of these were duds, but some started catching on. Sleepers began exchanging pictures of Donald Trump standing over a wall, or various cartoon figures sporting Donald Trump hats. The Virtual Adepts sat back like gardeners, helping to cultivate one meme here or squashing out another there. Some sleepers even started creating their own memes such as one of Jeb Bush wearing a guacamole bowl as a hat.<br /> <br /> These memes created powerful connections between tens of millions of sleepers, channeling their ideals into one. The consensus itself began to twist and warp due to the power of the dank memes populated by green frogs that the Virtual Adepts were using. Donald Trump's comment of Jeb Bush as &quot;low energy&quot; became a meme of its own and the Adepts cheered when the Technocracy's anointed candidate was knocked out of the race.<br /> <br /> As Donald Trump, buoyed by the power of millions of memes created and spread by sleepers crushed one opponent and then another, the Technocracy attempted to create its own memes to counteract those of the Virtual Adepts. However their attempt at #cruzmissile and others failed horribly, forcing them to admit that their understanding of memes was at least a decade behind the Adepts. And yet, they soon came to discover that the Adepts had also underestimated the power and danger of memes as well.<br /> <br /> It was only towards the end of the Republican Primary, the Virtual Adepts slowly began to realize that they had created a monster. The memes began to run out of control as sleepers took them, re-purposed them and like Pandora, the Virtual Adepts discovered that they could not put the memes back in the box.<br /> <br /> After Donald Trump's nomination as the Republican candidate, the Adepts could do nothing more than sit back in a state of shock and awe at the power of unchecked memes. By all that was right in the world, there was simply no way that Donald Trump should have won the Republican Primary. And yet, the power of meme magic had so twisted and warped the consensus that it had become fact, and worse, it meant that President Donald Trump might even be plausible.<br /> <br /> It was then that the Virtual Adepts began splintering. Quite a few were horrified at the thought of Donald Trump successfully winning. Many older Adepts lobbied strongly against Trump, his election cycle reminding them too much of the election which had occurred in Germany in 1933. These Adepts started trying to rally behind Bernie Sanders, using their memes to help him win, but it was too little too late. The Adepts had spent too much time focused Trump and by the time they tried to shift their efforts the Democratic Primary was already over.<br /> <br /> The Adepts found themselves split. Donald Trump was a danger, but there was no doubt that Hillary's globalist policies and positions favored the Technocracy. When Hillary Clinton's emails emerged, many Virtual Adepts were upset to find that she was so closely allied with the Technocracy than they had ever imagined. Indeed, some of the material left the Adepts wondering if perhaps she was not even more of a Technocratic candidate than Jeb Bush had been, an &quot;insurance&quot; candidate that regardless of whoever won the election, the Technocracy would be the ultimate winner.<br /> <br /> This was the moment when the Virtual Adepts fell into something of a civil war. Different Adepts threw their full weight behind one candidate or another, using memes, hacks and any other method they could to hurt the other candidate. The Technocracy and the NWO in particular, found their hands full dealing with the out-of-control memes unleashed by the Adepts on both sides.<br /> <br /> Then, on November 9th, many Adepts woke up to find themselves in a new world. Their memes had helped drive the most unlikely candidate in the history of American politics into the position of president. A chaos candidate had won. Through their actions and the power of meme magic, they had permanently twisted the consensus and yet they did not know whether they should cheer or should weep.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Just for those who are curious, <a href=\"http://motherboard.vice.com/read/trumps-occult-online-supporters-believe-pepe-meme-magic-got-him-elected\" target=\"_blank\">meme magic is kind of an actual ironic thing</a> that some people talk about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-18-2016, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T17:47:44-08:00","id":1004722,"title":"","content":"I was wondering when someone would start talking politics on here. Thought it would have been me at one point, but this is far more intricate than what I might have come up with.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is actually quite a cool little scenario, my only gripe is that there's not nearly enough Syndicate. The News Media had a tremendous role in the real life Trump campaign, so to disregard that is to ignore a crucial part of this story. The problem with real life meme culture is that it's fairly cyclical. On social media people tend to ignore things they don't agree with, and may even unfriend of block people who are consistently expressing opinions they don't like. This leads to all kinds of echo chambers being formed, which I think the idea of Virtual Adept civil war captures quite well. But the Web was not the primary medium by which the memes took hold, that was the news.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate have a finger in almost every news outlet across the country, with all kinds of orders directing spin and trying to guide the thoughts of the masses for one goal or another. Some members would be in it for the dollars, Trump was a great attraction to their networks, so the more they focused on him, the higher the ratings would sore. All the easier to advertise and sell. This made Trump the greatest news source since Brexit (and believe me, I'll get to that). This plays in to the not so subtle feud that's been going on between the NWO and the Syndicate for almost two decades now, with NWO trying desperately to keep they Syndicate's Press Spin companies in check while trying to do damage control on the VA's attacks. This could be one of the reasons contributing to their lack of efficacy against the less distracted VAs.<br /> <br /> However, once Trump got the nomination, the mood shifted quickly. Brexit was not too long ago, but it was a major shock to the system. It started out as a power play. NWO was doing business as usual with crowd control, but certain high ranking officials of the Syndicate were starting to get a bit tired of NWO calling all the shots and proudly proclaiming how much control they had over the masses. So they thought they'd stretch their propaganda muscles and show these glorified civil servants just who holds the sway here. The Brexit vote seemed the perfect vehicle for this. They didn't really expect a majority leave vote, they just wanted to make it close enough to prove the point. Unfortunately their point was proved far too well. Two NWO, the EU represents a small aspect of the socialist ideal, a network of nations where information and resources are easily shared and distributed. The Syndicate too benefited out of this arangement, but had to make a great number of compromises with NWO in order for it to function, of which many members are split about the costs vs the benefit. The prospect of the UK leaving the EU would threaten the stability of the experiment and potentially result in a cascade of other departures, destroying all the networks they had been setting up. This had to be avoided at all costs<br /> <br /> Minutes after the result came out, Syndicate officials tried to control the fallout by moving as much money as they could out of the UK and into safer stores. NWO started doing mass investigations all over the place to see who was behind such insubordination, as well as doing everything within its power to block Brexit and temper public opinion of the whole thing. It's been a long drawn out series of damage control measures, all while keeping the illusions that this was a free choice made by the masses.<br /> <br /> The Trump Incident was fast becoming another Brexit in the eyes of the Syndicate. While there were members who were quite up for another NWO vs Syndicate power struggle to put them in their place, others were not so gung-ho about it. They recognised that this infighting would threaten the Union and everything the Union was working towards up to this point. Furthermore, while no one quite predicted what a destabilising force a Leave vote for Brexit turned out to be, no one was under any illusions just how important the USA Executive Office was, and how badly they needed to maintain control of this. The Syndicate started going on the offensive, producing poll after poll demonstrating Clinton as the winner, trying to get as much dirt on Trump in the public eye, but it was too little too late, the damage had been done, accelerated by the VA assault.<br /> <br /> Perhaps because NWO and Syndicate didn't properly coordinate their attempts, perhaps because there were still members of the Syndicate that would rather a business man be president that another NWO puppet, or perhaps simply because they had both spectacularly underestimated the strength of will within the masses. Heads are going to roll for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T21:17:43-08:00","id":1004800,"title":"","content":"And at the center of this shadow war, Donald Trump ran his campaign unaware. The Syndicate was certainly interested in exploiting the press coverage he made, but they'd never go so far as to claim him as one of their own. Moreover, he's not subtle enough to be a Nephandi. Most likely, Trump is just a regular Sleeper.<br /> <br /> A Sleeper with two mundane but disturbingly potent talents: selling his own brand, and telling people what they want to hear.<br /> <br /> The Trump brand - that of an affluent and successful businessman (despite his numerous bankruptcies) - benefited enormously from the Meme War 2016, both from memes for and against him. It is said all publicity is good publicity, and Trump certainly proved the adage accurate. More importantly, perhaps, those memes drew attention to him specifically, over any other Republican candidate. Voters knew about Trump's candidacy more than any other Republican combined. So when he started spouting vague populist rhetoric, it resonated with the frustrations of the common Sleeper. For all his inexperience in politics, Trump was a master of the simplest campaign tactic: make promises that voters like. And he made a lot of promises (which Mages on every side will learn to bemoan in the coming years).<br /> <br /> On a wider scale, though, Trump's resonance with voters had an effect on the Consensus itself. For decades, the Democrat/Republican divide was the law of US political belief. It was a dichotomy so iron clad, it stymied repeated attempts by third parties to disrupt the status quo. The Technocracy saw to that, as a strict Us Vs. Them world view was easiest to control. It was so strong, it prevented the Republican party from disowning Trump, despite his numerous personal and policy deficiencies. They couldn't break out of the mindset that they needed to close ranks and support their own. But Trump wasn't really theirs; he was the self-styled Outsider, bringing the existing political establishment into conflict with a potent and dangerous Paradigm shift.<br /> <br /> Yes, the sleeper voters now had another option, the bastard offspring of the old Consensus and a burgeoning new one. The Meme War served to strengthen this, until the memes became self-sustaining. After a while, it didn't matter how tarnished Trump's actual character became under real scrutiny. His personal brand - writ in Trump gold - sat at the center of a maelstrom of belief, positive and negative. At the beginning of his campaign, a Trump victory was laughable. Not just because Trump was a clown and a snake oil salesmen, but because the Consensus wouldn't allow for an Outsider to win the presidency. At worst, it would split the Republican vote somehow (as such things had played out before), and the Democrats would win.<br /> <br /> At the end of the election, currents of altered belief swept the man into the White House. The unprecedented had happened, and the Consensus would never be the same again.<br /> <br /> The shock of that result almost certainly Awakened several people throughout the US and abroad, in a sudden moment of horror and worldview shattering confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T14:35:29-08:00","id":1009053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004643-what-really-happened-during-the-2016-election?p=1004800#post1004800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And at the center of this shadow war, Donald Trump ran his campaign unaware. The Syndicate was certainly interested in exploiting the press coverage he made, but they'd never go so far as to claim him as one of their own. Moreover, he's not subtle enough to be a Nephandi. Most likely, Trump is just a regular Sleeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Idunno\u2026 I think a case could be made for calling him a Syndic-gone-Marauder. Think about it: a lack of subtlety, and a tendency for tried-and-true PR procedures to backfire when aimed at him\u2026<br /> <br /> Except\u2026 the unspoken (and thus unquestioned) assumption here is that the Trump election is viewed with abject horror by just about everyone with half a brain (except the Nephandi, who are laughing hysterically from the sidelines). If you back away from the notion that his election is an unmitigated disaster that nobody reasonable wanted, what possibilities open up? <br /> <br /> What about the possibility of a faction of Traditionists who aimed for this outcome precisely because it shakes up the Consensus and has the Sleepers questioning their long-cherished assumptions about what is and isn't possible? I could see them reasoning that the dangers of a Trump presidency are manageable and/or an acceptable cost for the benefits of shaking the Sleepers out of their complacency. In the short term, they'll probably suffer a backlash from the rest of the Traditions; whether that becomes a long-term rift depends in part on whether or not Trump's administration turns out to be as bad as so many fear it will. Right now, it's too early to tell.<br /> <br /> Having the Celestial Chorus play a significant role in that faction would reflect the fact that a surprising amount of Trump's support came from the evangelical community; but I could also see a strong showing from the Etherites (though given how heavily tech-focused this scenario is already, I don't know how much I'd want to play up their role here). Maybe the Order of Hermes as well, simply due to the fact that they're the Tradition most likely to get caught up in politics.<br /> <br /> Conversely, if you want to play up the apocalyptic overtones that many see in this election, maybe this is the trigger for the much-anticipated Technocratic Civil War. As recriminations are tossed around about who let this happen, Control moves to reinstate its dominance and starts a witch-hunt within the Front Lines' ranks; and things snowball from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T14:59:03-08:00","id":1009059,"title":"","content":"Basically this is what happens when White Supremacists become Mages....<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://pre11.deviantart.net/c13c/th/pre/i/2016/330/6/c/old_king_kek_by_spearhafoc-dapq11l.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Occult (Villains): Meme Magick. This is Old King Kek (Doug Taylor).<br /> <br /> This one was directly inspired by an article I read in Motherboard about Meme Magicians who claim credit for Donald Trump's electoral victory: (<a href=\"http://www.deviantart.com/users/outgoing?http://motherboard.vice.com/read/trumps-occult-online-supporters-believe-pepe-meme-magic-got-him-elected?utm_source=mbfb\" target=\"_blank\">motherboard.vice.com/read/trum\u2026</a>)<br /> <br /> Meme Magick involves charging a symbol and letting it loose on the world, allowing it to shape reality. The Meme Magicians supporting Donald Trump supposedly used the character of Pepe the Frog, which had already become popular on sites like Tumblr and elsewhere, and used it as a sigil to bring about their desired goals (including White Nationalism, Antifeminism, and so on). They connected this character to an Egyptian god named Kek, usually represented as a man with a frog's head. Kek was a disruptive deity, and the Meme Magicians view him as a sort of &quot;God of Internet Trolls&quot;. The world &quot;Kek&quot; had already been a separate meme relating to the video game World of Warcraft, where it's the Orcish equivalent of &quot;LOL&quot;, making the supposed synchronicity impossible to resist for them.<br /> <br /> In doing further research, I came across a site managed by members of the self-described Alt-Right (the preferred term for modern White Nationalism) who connect Pepe/Kek with the understanding of Hinduism that had become somewhat popular in the Nazi party during WWII. There's a whole lot of nonsense, but essentially they describe spreading these ideas as &quot;meme-up\u0101ya&quot; (skillful memes). The ideas themselves are called &quot;kek-dharma&quot;, which they compare to the concept of the &quot;redpill&quot; popular among the so-called Men's Rights movement (It should be noted that the red pill concept was borrowed by The Matrix films, the brainchild of two left-leaning Transwomen). Kek here manifests himself as his avatar Pepe, who is a bodhisattva - or spiritual leader.<br /> <br /> There are various numbers associated with Neonazi Meme Magick that I included in the image. The number 7 is considered lucky, and online posts ending in it are considered to hold more weight than others; 666, of course, represents Satan and the Beast of Revelation; and 1488, tattooed on his knuckles, is a popular code among modern racists (14 represents the &quot;14 words&quot;, a White Nationalist motto, and 88 stands for HH, or &quot;Heil Hitler&quot;).<br /> <br /> This character is a real-life Internet troll who uses his Magick to sew fear and chaos, and spread his message of hate.<br /> <br /> Art style inspired by Matt Furie, who created the original Pepe character (it should be noted he is firmly against what has been done with his character by Trump's supporters and the White Nationalist movement). </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Link: <a href=\"http://www.deviantart.com/art/Old-King-Kek-647866569\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.deviantart.com/art/Old-King-Kek-647866569</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-27-2016, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T15:11:43-08:00","id":1009063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004643-what-really-happened-during-the-2016-election?p=1009053#post1009053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having the Celestial Chorus play a significant role in that faction would reflect the fact that a surprising amount of Trump's support came from the evangelical community; but I could also see a strong showing from the Etherites (though given how heavily tech-focused this scenario is already, I don't know how much I'd want to play up their role here). Maybe the Order of Hermes as well, simply due to the fact that they're the Tradition most likely to get caught up in politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hesitant to put any Tradition fully behind Trump, if we assume they did at all. Yes, many Evangelical Christians supported Trump (a fact that fills me, a Christian, with shame). But there are likely many other Christian Choristers who find the man's moral failings repugnant and unacceptable. And then there are all the other religious factions populating the Celestial Chorus. Muslim Choristers are probably positively livid right now, and the Monists can't be happy with so much widening of the gap between faiths.<br /> <br /> My money says the election rocked (and continues to rock) the Celestial Chorus, with increased tensions between groups. A Tradition divided against itself, with the peace-makers in the organization trying to prevent another Mercy Schism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T18:26:40-08:00","id":1009108,"title":"","content":"First, I wasn't suggesting that any tradition would be fully behind Trump. Second, while I'm also not happy with how evangelicals voted, I also haven't bought into the \u201cTrump is the second coming of Hitler\u201d narrative. So I tend to feel more disappointed and sad than ashamed. To me, the Trump victory boys and imperfect outcome, but far from the worst thing that could have happened. I figure that in this scenario, there should be others who tend to have a similar view. As opposed to the current version where version where everyone who is sane considers his win to be a major disaster.<br /> <br /> Third, I do agree that the celestial chorus is likely to experience a split over this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T19:58:53-08:00","id":1009137,"title":"","content":"I think we should first look at what caused Trump's rise in the real world, and then look at what the Mage equivalents would be.<br /> <br /> In the real world, economic stagnation and job loss resulted in large numbers of people in key states becoming deeply dissatisfied with the establishment. Some people saw the establishment as serving the interests of corporations rather than the common people. Others blamed immigrants and minorities for their misfortune, and blamed the establishment for not suppressing immigration and the growth of minorities. These two groups technically had little in common, one being liberal and the other right-wing, but their shared contempt for the establishment made them accidental allies, at least at the voting booth.<br /> <br /> The establishment fought hard to get establishment candidates on the final ticket. On the left, the establishment pushed Hillary Clinton, narrowly succeeding in getting her over Bernie Sanders. On the right, the establishment pushed first Jeb Bush, then a variety of acceptable alternatives, but ultimately failed to get an establishment candidate in. Trump was in most respects an awful politician, but he at least was saying anti-establishment things, whether he believed them or not.<br /> <br /> The election then came down to a referendum on the establishment. Hillary Clinton was widely perceived as being everything many people hated about the establishment: robotic, disconnected from the common man, in service to corporatism rather than democracy, and full of nitpicky PC outrage. This combination destroyed any enthusiasm for her on the left, and made her absolutely hated on the right. This guaranteed that many of the liberals energized by Bernie Sanders would simply stay home. And energized those on the right to vote as much out of hate for her as any affection for Trump.<br /> <br /> Had Trump been a better candidate, he probably would have crushed her. Instead he stuck his foot in his mouth constantly. But at least he was saying anti-establishment things, in a year when the establishment was viewed as the problem both by liberals and conservatives, albeit for different reasons: the left thinking the establishment was in the pocket of corporations, and the right thinking that the establishment wasn't protecting them from immigrants and minorities stealing their jobs.<br /> <br /> Had Trump been a better candidate, he would have crushed her. As is, he got just enough votes in key states to win the electoral college.<br /> <br /> Now from a Mage perspective, who are the equivalents here? The establishment is basically the Syndicate and NWO. They brought both parties under their control by first legalizing bribery in 1976 via their influence over the Supreme Court, declaring money to be a form of speech, and starting the process by which rich donors would become more important to both parties than the common man.<br /> <br /> Then they started to advance an agenda of globalism. As usual with the Technocracy, this was done out of a mix of noble and evil intentions. They wanted to move towards one world, where there is no war and everyone is equal. But also towards a world in which they control everything. Regardless of their motives, the common man gradually perceived that politicians where little more than robots(and in Mage some politicians might literally be robots) controlled by small elites completely disconnected from the daily lives of the common man.<br /> <br /> This created a backlash that gave birth to both Bernie Sanders' and Trump's movements, and their attempts to contain that backlash only stopped Sanders. Trump therefore is the result of a backlash, and may in part even be the result of a literal paradox backlash against the Syndicate and NWO's combined efforts to control everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 11-27-2016, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T05:15:39-08:00","id":1009285,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> Which either subtly implies that NWO are much better than Syndicate at influencing vote results since they managed to get their preferred candidate in the voting seat. Or that members of the Syndicate were pushing away from NWO desired &quot;politics as usual&quot; in order to show their strength, and then realised just how much they stood to lose when things got far too out of hand to curtail. Perhaps both to some extent are true.<br /> <br /> I think one thing we can agree on is that to the NWO, this election was a disaster, and the next couple of years are going to be a slew of manipulations in order to assure damage control, as well as calculated worldwide events to try and exacerbate his failings and undermine any faith the masses might have had with him. Syndicate are a much more complicated story, some may follow NWO's lead, others may oppose it. For example, one of the things Trump wants to do is put an end to Net Neutrality. This would be an amazing thing for the Syndicate who would finally be able to profit on the very gears of the modern world directly, rather than just through advertising. It would also severely limit the effects of Virtual Adepts (though knowing them, they'd probably set up their own networks independent of most Service Providers, so it would be a bit of a moot point). All these differing viewpoints very well could be one of the trigger points for a covert civil war under the guise of negotiation.<br /> <br /> What do the Void Engineers, Progenitors, and Iterators think about all this? Considering how Anti-intelectualist Trump seems to be, undermining a lot of their efforts. Progenitors are going to have a lot of problems with his &quot;Anti-Vaxer&quot; stance as vaccines are their most potent weapon against disease, and their greatest method of mass injections of experimental procedures. Void Engineers and Iterators are likely to be less effected. Iterators may even see a boost in funding as weapon stocks are starting to increase worldwide. Though it's true the VE have never really been all that concerned with the happenings on Earth these days.<br /> <br /> As for the traditions, I think a lot of them would be pretty disinterested in Sleeper Politics. Verbena, Dreamspeakers, Akashic's, and Ecstatics, for example, probably couldn't care less. Some may be clued up on how certain things affect them and their interests, but for the most part they'd probably think &quot;all politics are just the Technocracy anyway&quot; and leave it at that. Certainly the Akashics would be much more concerned with the acts of the CCP (Chinese Communist Party) and the threat on their territories than anything happening in the USA right now. As will many members of Euthanatos. Though there's always a chance that certain members of Trump's cabinet may become a target if the need arises.<br /> <br /> Order of Hermes would most likely keep to themselves, though those who influence sleeper politics would definitely be aware of all the goings on, and may even have had a hand in pushing Trump over the top in order to directly harm the Technocracy and the Technocratic ideal. They'd especially love his anti-intelecualism as a selling point, as more criticism brought on the Technocratic ideal can only mean a greater acceptance on that which the sleepers once denied whole heatedly.<br /> <br /> The Choristers would definitely be split. The Septarians would agree with a lot of his claims, and many of them may even be in favour of Pence and his ideas. Though almost everyone else would be at odds with this, especially the Islamic sector of the Chorus who are under threat more than ever before.<br /> <br /> The Etherites, however, would be a lot more tricky to determine. They usually keep to themselves after all, walled away in the world of lost academia. Some may not even be aware an election just took place. Others might be either for or against it but only in very specific ways.<br /> <br /> How does that sync up with what everyone else thinks of these traditions? And how do you think the Batini would respond to all of this? Perhaps now is their time to stop being silent...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T10:07:22-08:00","id":1009382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004643-what-really-happened-during-the-2016-election?p=1009285#post1009285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> Which either subtly implies that NWO are much better than Syndicate at influencing vote results since they managed to get their preferred candidate in the voting seat. Or that members of the Syndicate were pushing away from NWO desired &quot;politics as usual&quot; in order to show their strength, and then realised just how much they stood to lose when things got far too out of hand to curtail. Perhaps both to some extent are true.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeh, in this story you'd have to dump the idea tha the Syndicate and NWO are rivals, because their real-world equivalents were in lockstep. Both had worked together to gain control over the both the Republicans and Democrats, forming a single Establishment that mainly answered to big-money, and were advancing a globalist agenda mainly out of a desire to pay First-World workers as poorly as Third-World workers.<br /> <br /> For once, the WOD version of events would actually be nicer, at least in motives, than the real-world. In the WOD, Technocrats advanced a globalist agenda with the intent of gradually raising Third World workers to the level of First World Workers. That this caused First World workers to drop in pay to the level of Third World workers, or lose their jobs entirely, was just a short-term side-effect. The Technocracy did not foresee just how violently First World workers would react to this temporary side-effect, latching onto anyone who would save them from poverty, be it Sanders or Trump. The result was a massive rejection of the Establishment that the Syndicate and the NWO had worked together so flawlessly to create.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 11-28-2016, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T15:56:34-08:00","id":1009524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004643-what-really-happened-during-the-2016-election?p=1009382#post1009382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eeeh, in this story you'd have to dump the idea tha the Syndicate and NWO are rivals, because their real-world equivalents were in lockstep. Both had worked together to gain control over the both the Republicans and Democrats, forming a single Establishment that mainly answered to big-money, and were advancing a globalist agenda mainly out of a desire to pay First-World workers as poorly as Third-World workers.<br /> <br /> For once, the WOD version of events would actually be nicer, at least in motives, than the real-world. In the WOD, Technocrats advanced a globalist agenda with the intent of gradually raising Third World workers to the level of First World Workers. That this caused First World workers to drop in pay to the level of Third World workers, or lose their jobs entirely, was just a short-term side-effect. The Technocracy did not foresee just how violently First World workers would react to this temporary side-effect, latching onto anyone who would save them from poverty, be it Sanders or Trump. The result was a massive rejection of the Establishment that the Syndicate and the NWO had worked together so flawlessly to create.</div> </div> </div> </div>This being part of the Technocracy's hubris. They were so convinced of the rightness of their plans, and so distant from the Sleepers, it never occurred to them that the common man would possibly object. That the &quot;short term side effects&quot; in the eyes of the manipulators of mankind would look like &quot;immediate life-ruining problems&quot; to the person living paycheck to paycheck. The Technocrats either can't see the effects their work causes on the people on the ground, or else don't acknowledge the severity of those effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T09:38:22-08:00","id":1010231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004643-what-really-happened-during-the-2016-election?p=1009285#post1009285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> Which either subtly implies that NWO are much better than Syndicate at influencing vote results since they managed to get their preferred candidate in the voting seat. Or that members of the Syndicate were pushing away from NWO desired &quot;politics as usual&quot; in order to show their strength, and then realised just how much they stood to lose when things got far too out of hand to curtail. Perhaps both to some extent are true.<br /> <br /> I think one thing we can agree on is that to the NWO, this election was a disaster, and the next couple of years are going to be a slew of manipulations in order to assure damage control, as well as calculated worldwide events to try and exacerbate his failings and undermine any faith the masses might have had with him. Syndicate are a much more complicated story, some may follow NWO's lead, others may oppose it. For example, one of the things Trump wants to do is put an end to Net Neutrality. This would be an amazing thing for the Syndicate who would finally be able to profit on the very gears of the modern world directly, rather than just through advertising. It would also severely limit the effects of Virtual Adepts (though knowing them, they'd probably set up their own networks independent of most Service Providers, so it would be a bit of a moot point). All these differing viewpoints very well could be one of the trigger points for a covert civil war under the guise of negotiation.<br /> <br /> What do the Void Engineers, Progenitors, and Iterators think about all this? Considering how Anti-intelectualist Trump seems to be, undermining a lot of their efforts. Progenitors are going to have a lot of problems with his &quot;Anti-Vaxer&quot; stance as vaccines are their most potent weapon against disease, and their greatest method of mass injections of experimental procedures. Void Engineers and Iterators are likely to be less effected. Iterators may even see a boost in funding as weapon stocks are starting to increase worldwide. Though it's true the VE have never really been all that concerned with the happenings on Earth these days.<br /> <br /> As for the traditions, I think a lot of them would be pretty disinterested in Sleeper Politics. Verbena, Dreamspeakers, Akashic's, and Ecstatics, for example, probably couldn't care less. Some may be clued up on how certain things affect them and their interests, but for the most part they'd probably think &quot;all politics are just the Technocracy anyway&quot; and leave it at that. Certainly the Akashics would be much more concerned with the acts of the CCP (Chinese Communist Party) and the threat on their territories than anything happening in the USA right now. As will many members of Euthanatos. Though there's always a chance that certain members of Trump's cabinet may become a target if the need arises.<br /> <br /> Order of Hermes would most likely keep to themselves, though those who influence sleeper politics would definitely be aware of all the goings on, and may even have had a hand in pushing Trump over the top in order to directly harm the Technocracy and the Technocratic ideal. They'd especially love his anti-intelecualism as a selling point, as more criticism brought on the Technocratic ideal can only mean a greater acceptance on that which the sleepers once denied whole heatedly.<br /> <br /> The Choristers would definitely be split. The Septarians would agree with a lot of his claims, and many of them may even be in favour of Pence and his ideas. Though almost everyone else would be at odds with this, especially the Islamic sector of the Chorus who are under threat more than ever before.<br /> <br /> The Etherites, however, would be a lot more tricky to determine. They usually keep to themselves after all, walled away in the world of lost academia. Some may not even be aware an election just took place. Others might be either for or against it but only in very specific ways.<br /> <br /> How does that sync up with what everyone else thinks of these traditions? And how do you think the Batini would respond to all of this? Perhaps now is their time to stop being silent...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with this in most ways, especially from the Technocracy end of things, but I think you're forgetting just how radical an increase in white nationalist ideologies receiving influence and public attention was associated with the Trump campaign. This will almost certainly ruffle the feathers of more than a few Dreamspeakers, especially those of a Native American or Mesoamerican background. Meanwhile, some Traditions have been shown to contain alarmingly vocal white supremicist factions *cough* Verbena and to a lesser extent Etherites*cough*; skeletons in their respective Tradition's closets that seem prepared to rear their heads once more.<br /> <br /> As far as other fallout from the election go, I think the Virtual Adepts are only beginning to wake up to how much they've shot themselves in the foot via Trump's net neutrality policy. The Euthanatos aren't likely to pass judgement yet (at least on an organizational basis). I can't help but imagine that the Order of Hermes sees the whole affair as nothing more than squabbling within the Technocracy and are inclined to withhold judgement for the moment as well. The mainline (read: non-racist) portions of the Verbena and the Sons of Ether are likely absolutely terrified, given the former's environmentalist stance and feminist tendencies and the latter's love of alternative energy and quasi-socialist leanings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T12:42:31-08:00","id":1011620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004643-what-really-happened-during-the-2016-election?p=1009524#post1009524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This being part of the Technocracy's hubris. They were so convinced of the rightness of their plans, and so distant from the Sleepers, it never occurred to them that the common man would possibly object. That the &quot;short term side effects&quot; in the eyes of the manipulators of mankind would look like &quot;immediate life-ruining problems&quot; to the person living paycheck to paycheck. The Technocrats either can't see the effects their work causes on the people on the ground, or else don't acknowledge the severity of those effects.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They also underestimate the perceptiveness of the common people somewhat. They thought that once they managed to make bribery legal in 1976, that was it, democracy was over, they could control the message the common people would recieve, because they could control both the Republican arguments and the Democratic counter-arguments, turning any debate between Republicans and Democrats into just a game of Good-Cop/Bad-Cop that advanced the Establishment agenda. But people saw through it, at least partially. They didn't have the political expertise to respond to it in a healthy way, but they could certainly try to vomit up the corruption.<br /> <br /> That's what the wild shift's in congress over the past few decades could be considered: an attempt by Democracy to vomit up the corruption killing it. But you can't vomit up cancer. That requires surgery. In this case, surgery would be something like an amendment making bribery illegal again. But the establishment has been able to keep that off the table. So democracy just keeps vomiting again and again, making congress lurch from Democrat to Republican and back again to no avail.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T13:03:39-08:00","id":1011624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004643-what-really-happened-during-the-2016-election?p=1011620#post1011620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what the wild shift's in congress over the past few decades could be considered: an attempt by Democracy to vomit up the corruption killing it. But you can't vomit up cancer. That requires surgery. In this case, surgery would be something like an amendment making bribery illegal again. But the establishment has been able to keep that off the table. So democracy just keeps vomiting again and again, making congress lurch from Democrat to Republican and back again to no avail.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds strangely like something a Progenitor would say...<br /> Perhaps they had more to do with this than they first appeared!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}